==English==

[[File:Cicada_molting_animated-2.gif|thumb|A cicada molting.]]

===Alternative forms===
* [[moult]] (''British English'')

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|mouten}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} *''mutian'' (cf. {{m|ang|bemutian}}), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|muto|mūtō, mūtāre}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/moʊlt/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/mɒlt/|lang=en}}{{rfv-pronunciation|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/məʊlt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊlt|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[shed]] hair, feathers, skin, horns etc. and replace it by a fresh layer.
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To shed in such a manner.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|To shed hair, feathers, skin, horns etc., as an animal}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|luoda}}, {{t+|fi|pudottaa}}
* French: {{t+|fr|muer}}
