* Hungarian: {{t|hu|vedlik}}
* Icelandic: {{qualifier|of insects and reptiles}} {{t|is|hleypa hömum}}, {{qualifier|of birds}} {{t|is|fella fjaðrir}}, {{qualifier|of cats and dogs}} {{t|is|fara úr hárum}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Russian: {{t+|ru|линять}}
* Spanish: {{t|es|pelechar}}
* Swedish: {{t+|sv|ömsa}}, {{t|sv|rugga}}
{{trans-bottom}}

{{trans-top|To shed in such a manner (transitive form)}}
* French: {{t+|fr|muer}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Swedish: {{t+|sv|ömsa}}, {{t|sv|rugga}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The process of shedding or losing a covering of [[fur]], [[feather]]s or [[skin]] etc.
#: ''Some birds change colour during their winter '''molt'''.''
# The skin or feathers cast off during the process of [[#Verb|molt]]ing.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|The skin or feathers cast off during the process of molting}}
* French: {{t+|fr|mue|f}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Icelandic: {{qualifier|of insects and reptiles}} {{t|is|hamskipti|n-p}}, {{qualifier|of birds}} {{t|is|fjaðrafellir|m}}
{{trans-bottom}}

